"""Language edit of the Results paragraphs in outputs/results_blocks_main.json. Run after script 82. Every paragraph is matched by its opening words, and every number is kept.
Interpretation that sat in the Results was removed from the cluster filter paragraph, where the Discussion already carries it."""
import json, os, re
B = r'.'; P = os.path.join(B, 'outputs', 'results_blocks_main.json')
blocks = json.load(open(P, encoding='utf-8'))
NEW = {
 'Vegetation or rangeland occupied 3411.37': "Vegetation or rangeland occupied 3411.37 km², bare soil or sand 814.11 km², cropland 336.43 km², built-up land 197.48 km² and water 21.42 km² (Table 3). Overall agreement with the 373 hold-out reference points was 0.90 with kappa 0.86. Producer's agreement was between 0.86 and 0.97 in every class except built-up land, at 0.25, and user's agreement was between 0.91 and 0.99 except for built-up land, at 0.06 (Table 3).",
 'The stratified sample drew 500 points': "The stratified sample drew 500 points for each class, and the spatial block split placed 417, 375, 408, 496 and 431 of them in training and 83, 125, 92, 4 and 69 in the hold-out for water, cropland, vegetation or rangeland, built-up land and bare soil or sand in that order (Table 3). Nearly all built-up points fell in blocks assigned to training, so the built-up values in Table 3 rest on 4 points. One of these was mapped as built-up and 3 as vegetation or rangeland, and 12 cropland hold-out points were mapped as built-up, which gives the producer's and user's agreement of 0.25 and 0.06 (Table S1). When each block was held out in turn, agreement with the consensus labels over 2500 points was 0.90 overall with kappa 0.87, and the producer's and user's agreement for built-up land were 0.81 and 0.88 on 500 points (Table 3). All of these values measure agreement with labels on which WorldCover and Dynamic World agreed and not accuracy against field observation.",
 'Of the 4780.81 km² of the study area': "Of the 4780.81 km² study area, 21.29 km² or 0.45% was excluded as permanent water and 1067.02 km² or 22.32% by the HAND and slope limits outside permanent water, which left an analysed area of 3692.49 km² or 77.24% (Table S2). The terrain limits removed 973.08 km² of vegetation or rangeland, 85.03 km² of bare soil or sand, 5.51 km² of cropland and 3.28 km² of built-up land. Flagged areas and class shares in the later sections refer to the analysed area. No pixel of the study rectangle had a missing HAND value, so setting missing values to 0 m changed nothing. The MERIT Hydro grid held 65656 pixels with a HAND of exactly 0 m inside the rectangle, all of them valid observations.",
 'Within an analysed area of 3692.49 km²': "Within an analysed area of 3692.49 km², the flagged area was 4.05 km² on 2 November, 225.84 km² on 14 November, 275.09 km² on 26 November and 208.70 km² on 8 December (Table 4). After 2 November, cropland held the largest flagged area on every date, at 92.15 km² on 14 November, 130.39 km² on 26 November and 97.90 km² on 8 December. Built-up land followed with 78.40, 84.20 and 50.67 km² on those dates, and bare soil or sand and vegetation or rangeland each held between 26.02 and 33.30 km². Water carried no analysed or flagged area.",
 'Expressed as a share of the analysed area': "As a share of the analysed area of each class, the flagged proportion on 14 November was 40.37% in built-up land, 27.85% in cropland, 4.01% in bare soil or sand and 1.07% in vegetation or rangeland, and 6.12% overall (Table 4). On 26 November the shares were 43.36% for built-up land, 39.40% for cropland, 4.57% for bare soil or sand and 1.12% for vegetation or rangeland, with 7.45% overall. By 8 December cropland was flagged most, at 29.58%, followed by built-up land at 26.09%, and the overall share was 5.65%. The overall share on 2 November was 0.11%.",
 'Of the 225.84 km² flagged on 14 November': "Of the 225.84 km² flagged on 14 November, 72.41 km² fell in the weak class of change in vertical transmit and vertical receive backscatter, ΔVV, 36.59 km² in the moderate class and 116.84 km² in the strong class (Table S4). The strong class was the largest in cropland, built-up land and bare soil or sand, at 50.79, 38.06 and 21.95 km². In vegetation or rangeland the weak class was the largest at 16.49 km², against 3.49 km² moderate and 6.04 km² strong.",
 'Counting the dates on which a pixel was flagged': "Counting the dates on which a pixel was flagged among 14 November, 26 November and 8 December, 102.87 km² was flagged on one date, 101.48 km² on two dates and 134.60 km² on all three (Table S4). Most of the flagged cropland, built-up land and bare soil or sand, at 65.66, 43.08 and 20.47 km², was flagged on all three dates, whereas most of the flagged vegetation or rangeland, 44.85 km², was flagged on a single date.",
 'Against the Pléiades mapping of 12 November': "Against the Pléiades mapping of 12 November, the final rule reached precision, recall, balanced accuracy and kappa of 0.72, 0.70, 0.79 and 0.58, compared with 0.67, 0.72, 0.78 and 0.54 without the cluster filter and 0.37, 0.88, 0.59 and 0.14 for the fixed thresholds (Figure 6 and Table S5). Outside the calibration extent, the Gaofen-2 mapping of 23 November gave 0.92, 0.56, 0.76 and 0.53 for the final rule, 0.87, 0.57, 0.75 and 0.51 without the cluster filter and 0.56, 0.85, 0.64 and 0.27 for the fixed thresholds. The WorldView-2 mapping of 30 November gave values within 0.01 of these for the first two rules and 0.56, 0.85, 0.63 and 0.26 for the fixed thresholds. Over the whole extent of each mapping, precision of the calibrated rules stayed above 0.90 and kappa lay between 0.41 and 0.44, against a kappa of 0.24 for the fixed thresholds.",
 'Agreement varied by ESA WorldCover class': "Agreement varied by ESA WorldCover class (Table 6). On the Pléiades date, precision and recall were 0.75 and 0.95 in cropland, 0.74 and 0.87 in grassland, 0.69 and 0.81 in shrubland, 0.57 and 0.52 in tree cover and 0.89 and 0.26 in built-up land, against 0.04 and 0.34 in bare or sparse vegetation and 0.66 and 0.32 in permanent water bodies. For the Gaofen-2 mapping outside the calibration extent, recall was 0.71 in cropland and between 0.36 and 0.48 in grassland, shrubland and tree cover, but only 0.07 in built-up land and 0.04 in bare or sparse vegetation. Precision stayed above 0.90 in every vegetated or built-up class and fell to 0.33 in bare or sparse vegetation and 0.12 in permanent water bodies.",
 'The share of reference pixels that UNOSAT mapped': "The share of reference pixels that UNOSAT mapped as flooded was lower for smaller changes in backscatter (Figure S1). For the Pléiades and 14 November pair it was 0.84 where the change was below -12 dB, 0.85 between -12 and -9 dB, 0.83 between -9 and -7 dB, 0.73 between -7 and -5 dB, 0.58 between -5 and -4 dB, 0.46 between -4 and -3 dB, 0.30 between -3 and -2 dB, 0.16 between -2 and 0 dB and 0.17 above 0 dB. For the Gaofen-2 and 26 November pair the corresponding shares were 0.94, 0.93, 0.93, 0.92, 0.91, 0.83, 0.61, 0.30 and 0.24.",
 'On the calibration date, kappa rose': "On the calibration date, kappa rose from 0.544 with no cluster filter to 0.576 at a minimum cluster of 50 pixels, 0.580 at 100 and 200 pixels and 0.583 at 500 pixels (Table S7). Over the same sizes the flagged area in the scored part of the town fell from 15.06 km² to 12.77 km², precision rose from 0.67 to 0.74 and recall fell from 0.72 to 0.68.",
 'Within the scoring masks, the filter removed': "Within the scoring masks, the filter removed 1.47 km² of flagged area on the calibration date and 1.78 km² on each independent date outside the calibration extent (Table S9). Of the removed pixels, 18.8%, 30.9% and 30.8% lay inside the UNOSAT flood extent, against 72.1%, 92.3% and 92.4% of the retained pixels and 32.0%, 46.6% and 46.9% of the whole scoring mask. The removed pixels held 0.28, 0.55 and 0.55 km² of mapped flood, which was 2.0%, 1.6% and 1.6% of the flooded reference area. By cluster size, the flooded share of flagged pixels in clusters of 1 to 9, 10 to 49 and 50 to 99 pixels was 0.11, 0.16 and 0.32 on the calibration date and 0.23, 0.25 and 0.55 for the Gaofen-2 mapping outside the calibration extent (Table S9).",
 'Over the full area, the filter removed': "Over the full area, the filter removed 170.54 km² of the 396.37 km² flagged on 14 November without it, or 43.0% (Table S10). Of this, 139.28 km² lay in vegetation or rangeland, 19.98 km² in bare soil or sand, 7.06 km² in cropland and 4.22 km² in built-up land, which was 84.3%, 40.6%, 7.1% and 5.1% of the unfiltered flagged area of each class.",
 'The flagged area of 14 November was 225.8': "The flagged area of 14 November was 225.8 km² for the main configuration and 396.4 km² without the cluster filter (Table 7). Omitting the dark-surface exclusion gave 227.3 km², omitting the terrain mask gave 229.3 km² and a 3 by 3 filter gave 244.4 km². The rule using ΔVV alone gave 210.3 km². Using only the 9 October scene as the pre-event reference gave 185.1 km², whereas using only the 21 October scene gave 573.8 km². The fixed thresholds without a median filter gave 2187.8 km². Without the cluster filter the configurations gave between 282.7 and 2277.4 km².",
 'In the town, the main reference gave kappa': "In the town, the main reference gave kappa of 0.58 on the calibration date and 0.53 on both the Gaofen-2 and WorldView-2 mappings outside the calibration extent. The 9 October scene alone gave 0.54, 0.46 and 0.46, the 21 October scene alone 0.38, 0.56 and 0.56, and the 2 November scene alone 0.46, 0.63 and 0.63. The mean of 21 October and 2 November gave 0.46, 0.61 and 0.61, and the mean of all three scenes gave 0.57, 0.56 and 0.56 (Table 8).",
 'Over the extent of the town rasters': "Over the extent of the town rasters, the flagged area of 14 November without the terrain mask was 51.163 km² on a 10 m grid, 45.741 km² on a 20 m grid and 45.002 km² on a 30 m grid (Table S13). With the inputs reprojected to 10 m and the result summed on a 20 m grid it was 45.725 km², and the local implementation gave 51.163 km². The exported 10 m flag layer gave 51.123 km² over the same extent. Averaging the 10 m flag layer to 20 m gave 51.160 km². Sampling the inputs at 20 m before the 5 by 5 pixel filter gave 45.672 to 45.789 km² across the four sampling offsets. The 10 m rule gave 45.579 km² with a 9 by 9 pixel window and 44.839 km² with an 11 by 11 pixel window.",
}
done = 0
for x in blocks:
    if x['t'] != 'p': continue
    for k, v in NEW.items():
        if x['x'].startswith(k): x['x'] = v; done += 1; break
assert done == len(NEW), (done, len(NEW))
json.dump(blocks, open(P, 'w', encoding='utf-8'), ensure_ascii=False, indent=1); print('paragraphs rewritten', done)
